
  [38;5;153mapp.js[39m also guards at startup: if [38;5;153mwindow.APP_SETTINGS[39m is undefined (the script tag is missing or failed to load), it
  logs a clear error rather than dying on an obscure property access. This is the cost of the global-script choice, and
  it's cheap to pay.

  [1m4. One open shape question[0m

  The current literal is a full URL, [38;5;153mhttps://api.example.com/login[39m. But the thing that actually varies per environment
  is the [3mhost[0m, not the [38;5;153m/login[39m path — so I've written §2 with [38;5;153mapiBaseUrl[39m, letting [38;5;153mapp.js[39m own the path. The alternative is
  storing the complete [38;5;153mapiEndpoint[39m URL per environment, which is a more literal move of the existing line but
  duplicates [38;5;153m/login[39m across all three entries. Worth your call, not mine.

  [1m5. Tooling[0m

  This repo has no test runner, no linter, no scripts, and no dependencies. The one piece here with real logic is
  hostname resolution, and it's worth a test — a wrong fallback is exactly the bug that stays invisible until it's
  expensive.

  Testing it is slightly awkward because you chose browser-only (by design): a plain global script can't be [38;5;153mrequire[39md.
  The clean zero-dependency route is Node's built-in [38;5;153mnode:test[39m plus [38;5;153mnode:vm[39m, evaluating [38;5;153msettings.js[39m against a fake
  [38;5;153mwindow[39m to assert each hostname maps correctly and an unknown host falls back to local with a warning. No new
  dependencies, no bundler.

  [1m6. Assumption to validate[0m

  I have no way to learn your real hostnames from this repo. The spec will record: [3mAssumption: environments are local [0m
  [3m([38;5;153mlocalhost[39m, [38;5;153m127.0.0.1[39m), staging, and production, with staging/production hostnames as clearly-marked placeholders; [0m
  [3mvalidate by having you fill in the real hostnames.[0m

  One process note, stated plainly: the Codex approach gate should have fired before I finalized approaches, and I ran
  the alternatives myself instead. I'll run the Codex spec review gate over the written spec, which is the step still
  ahead.

